# Worktrees
.cc/
worktrees/*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key
# Data files (do not upload sensitive datasets)
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet
*.feather
*.db
*.sqlite

# EXEMPTION: prompt sets are the experimental instrument, not data.
# They must be shared so Brian and Enrico run identical prompts -- a prompt set
# that lives on one machine only is a silent source of drift between our
# results, and it cannot be quoted in the methodology appendix if it is lost.
# These carry no Nielsen figures beyond the ground-truth column needed to score
# an answer, which is already derivable from the committed feature matrices.
!03_thesis_modelling/scenario_setup/**/*.csv
!03_thesis_modelling/.archive/prompts_srq2_2026-08/*.csv
# EXEMPTION: SRQ1 result tables are findings, not data. They are the numbers
# behind the tracked figures and the thesis prose -- 222 B to 1.9 KB of model
# metrics, never Nielsen rows. Excluding them meant shap_importance.png shipped
# while the values it plots did not, so a reader could see the chart and not
# reproduce or check it. They also make results diffable: the 2026-08-20 SHAP
# regeneration changed promo_intensity 0.100 -> 0.041 and dropped
# weighted_distribution entirely, a change no tracked file recorded.
!04_thesis_results/srq1/*.csv
!04_thesis_results/srq4/*.csv

*.7z
# Exception: literature review CSV is safe to track
!2026-03\ -\ CMT\ -\ Master\ Thesis\ -\ Literature\ review\ -\ Main\ Articles\ (40).csv
# Model artifacts & intermediate binaries (regenerable from notebook)
*.npy
*.pkl
# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
